            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for the prime of youth, then the Hindi for to whimper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दूल्हा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूल्हा — dūlhā — \"a bridegroom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूल्हा घोड़े पर बैठकर आया। dūlhā ghoṛe par baiṭhkar āyā. The bridegroom arrived on horseback."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूल्हा (dūlhā) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Hindi dūlhā, \"bridegroom\", under Sanskrit durlabha, \"hard to get, precious\" (CDIAL 6446): the dear one. The bride is dulhan, the feminine of the same word, listed in the same entry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
