              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मेहंदी (mehndī) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Hindi mẽhdī, the henna plant, under Sanskrit mēndhī (CDIAL 10328). Its leaves are ground to a paste that leaves red-brown patterns on the hands, above all before a wedding."
            }
          ]
        },
