          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विदाई — vidāī — \"a farewell; the bride's leave-taking\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विदाई के समय मीरा और उसकी माँ दोनों रोईं। vidāī ke samay Mīrā aur uskī māṁ donõ roīṃ. At the bride's farewell, Mira and her mother both wept."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विदाई (vidāī) is vidā, \"farewell\", with the ending -ī; vidā is usually traced to Arabic vidāʿ, \"farewell\", which reached Hindi through Persian. At a wedding it is the moment the bride leaves her parents' home."
            }
          ]
        },
